<Task version="1.2" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/windows/2004/02/mit/task">
  <RegistrationInfo>
    <Description>Sotto warm engine - segura o grafo fora da shell para a primeira legenda nao pagar a carga (desenho: state/design/warm-worker-20261104.md)</Description>
  </RegistrationInfo>
  <!-- NO TRIGGERS, DELIBERATELY (R4). At logon this box reads `alta`/`muito-alta`
       (measured: _main/panel-visibility.json, `"shed": "muito-alta"`), and a
       graph load there is exactly the freeze the owner forbids. The engine is
       started ON DEMAND by `schtasks /run` when the box has an idle window, and
       G1 defers the load when it does not. -->
  <Triggers />
  <Principals>
    <Principal id="Author">
      <LogonType>InteractiveToken</LogonType>
      <RunLevel>LeastPrivilege</RunLevel>
    </Principal>
  </Principals>
  <Settings>
    <!-- Twin lock #1: a second `schtasks /run` starts nothing. -->
    <MultipleInstancesPolicy>IgnoreNew</MultipleInstancesPolicy>
    <DisallowStartIfOnBatteries>false</DisallowStartIfOnBatteries>
    <StopIfGoingOnBatteries>false</StopIfGoingOnBatteries>
    <AllowHardTerminate>true</AllowHardTerminate>
    <StartWhenAvailable>true</StartWhenAvailable>
    <RunOnlyIfNetworkAvailable>false</RunOnlyIfNetworkAvailable>
    <WakeToRun>false</WakeToRun>
    <AllowStartOnDemand>true</AllowStartOnDemand>
    <Enabled>true</Enabled>
    <Hidden>true</Hidden>
    <RunOnlyIfIdle>false</RunOnlyIfIdle>
    <!-- PT0S: the default 3-day limit would silently kill a warm engine and
         turn every boot after day 3 back into a cold boot (F14). -->
    <!-- O PT0S NAO E' UM TECTO, E' O DEFAULT DELETADO (medido 2026-11-15).
         A razao de cima continua verdadeira: os 3 DIAS do Task Scheduler matam
         um motor quente. Mas `PT0S` diz "sem limite nenhum", e um processo sem
         limite nenhum e' o actor que o watcher acusou DUAS vezes
         (`pythonw.exe(42792)` a **14,15 % da maquina** e, antes, **18,2 % /
         57 fios**). O numero tem de ser maior do que qualquer residencia
         legitima medida e menor do que "para sempre": medido
         `ms_resident=3 146 344` = **36,4 dias** (`_main/warm-engine.log`,
         release depois de uma residencia longa) e o TTL de parque e' 600 s
         (`WARM_PARK_TTL_S`). 14 dias = 1 209 600 s fica entre os dois: uma
         sessao real (horas) nunca o alcanca, e um motor esquecido com o dono
         fora por duas semanas nao continua a segurar ~1 GB.
         O motor que expira por este limite NAO perde trabalho: o TTL de 600 s
         ja' o teria expirado muito antes se estivesse parado, e se estiver a
         transcrever o reinicio seguinte volta a carregar em 6-9 s (medido:
         `WARM_LOAD_MS ms=6862.8`). -->
    <ExecutionTimeLimit>P14D</ExecutionTimeLimit>
    <!-- R3: a crash-looping engine must not become a load loop. Bounded at 2;
         the third crash leaves it ABSENT and says WARM_ENGINE_DIED. -->
    <RestartOnFailure>
      <Interval>PT60S</Interval>
      <Count>2</Count>
    </RestartOnFailure>
    <Priority>7</Priority>
  </Settings>
  <Actions Context="Author">
    <Exec>
      <Command>H:\sotto\_main\warm-engine\warm-engine-run.cmd</Command>
      <WorkingDirectory>H:\sotto\_main\warm-engine</WorkingDirectory>
    </Exec>
  </Actions>
</Task>
